==Bulgarian==

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|bg|sla-pro|*morje}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|bg}} {{m|ine-pro|*móri}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/moˈrɛ/|lang=bg}}

====Noun====
{{bg-noun|head=море́|g=n}}

# [[sea]], [[briny]]
# [[seaside]]
# {{lb|bg|figuratively}} [[thousands]] of, a [[wilderness]] of

=====Inflection=====
{{bg-noun-n-ta}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|el|bg}} {{m|el|μωρέ|sc=Grek}}, frozen vocative of {{m|el|μωρός|sc=Grek}}, meaning [[stupid]], but commonly used as a colloquial address.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ˈmɔrɛ/|lang=bg}}

====Particle====
{{head|bg|particle|head=мо́ре}}

# {{lb|bg|archaic}} [[you]], general vocative expression, used to augment an address

